   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing the\nvillage of Floral Park in the county of Nassau to establish a residential\nparking system",
    "basePrintNo": "S8953",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8953-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1640-r, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8953\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing\nthe village of Floral Park in the county of Nassau to establish a resi-\ndential parking system\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nto amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing the\nvillage of Floral Park in the county of Nassau to establish a residen-\ntial parking system.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends the vehicle and traffic law to authorize\nthe Village of Floral Park to adopt a residential parking permit system.\nSection two of the bill states that notwithstanding the provisions of\nany law to the contrary, the village board of the Village of Floral Park\nmay, by adoption of a local law or ordinance, provide for a residential\nparking permit system and fix and require the payment of the fees appli\ncable to parking within the area in which such parking system is in\neffect in accordance with the provisions of this section.\n\nSection three of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs a result of the redevelopment of the Belmont Park Racetrack, resi-\ndents who abide adjacent to the development site will be burdened with\nan influx of consumers and fans in their neighborhoods. The lack of\nparking for residents of certain areas of the Village of Floral Park,\nNassau county, has resulted in traffic hazards, congestion and air and\nnoise pollution. In addition, such lack of parking poses a hazard to\nresidents and other pedestrians in such areas. As such, a residential\nparking system would be in the public interest while reducing such\nhazards and pollution levels as well.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
